cost_estimate:
Spent in this exploration: 1,292,101 tokens (deepseek 1,127,286 over 395 cells; GLM 164,777 over 109 calls; 38 for the probe). All descriptive analyses were free.

Follow-ups (ESTIMATED from measured per-cell costs: SearchQA TC cell about 3.9k tokens; OfficeQA prompt about 7.0k plus completion; LiveMath about 3.4k plus 0.5k; ALFWorld TC episode about 105k prompt tokens):
- Length-predictability probe on SearchQA: GLM predicts the word count without the reference (60 calls, about 0.1M) plus one deepseek run (about 0.24M). Total about 0.35M.
- The same headroom probe (TC, oracle ×2, form, length, leak probes) on 60 failing items:
  - LiveMath: about 1.2M;
  - OfficeQA: about 2.5M (GLM hints on 20-30k-character pages about 10k each);
  - SpreadsheetBench: about 1M plus docker scoring;
  - ALFWorld: about 25M (impractical; use observational data instead).
- Detecting a +3-pt rule effect over the TC on SearchQA (between-text SD 0.22): about 420 items × 4 runs × 2 arms ≈ 13M tokens. Detecting +1.5 pts needs about 1,700 items, more than the 600-item pool.

